What are High Speed Train Bogies?
High Speed Train Bogies are critical undercarriage components that support the train's weight while ensuring stability, safety, and smooth operation at speeds exceeding 200 km/h. These bogies consist of wheel sets, suspension systems, and braking mechanisms engineered to withstand dynamic forces while maintaining passenger comfort. The two primary configurations are H-form bogies (known for structural rigidity) and O-form bogies (offering enhanced flexibility for varying track conditions).
